{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Two of every kind shall come to you, to keep alive</b> — He informed him that of their own accord they would come before him, two by two, and he would not need to hunt them in the mountains and islands, and afterward he would bring them into the ark. And in the narrative it explains that they came, male and female (Genesis 7:9), and this was included among them. Afterward He commanded him to take of every clean beast seven and seven, and concerning these He did not say that they would come to him, but rather that he would take them — for those that come to be saved and to keep seed alive come of themselves, but those that come to be offered as burnt offerings — He did not decree that they would come of themselves to be slaughtered, but rather Noah took them, for the command of seven and seven was so that Noah would be able to offer sacrifices from them. And the meaning of \"the clean\": the Holy One, blessed be He, explained to him the signs of purity, but Scripture abbreviates and says \"the clean\" according to the Torah. And Rashi wrote: \"that which is destined to be clean for Israel\" — this teaches that Noah studied Torah. Now, from here it follows that nothing was permitted for the offerings of the sons of Noah except clean beast and clean bird, and so it says concerning Hevel (Genesis 4:4): \"from the firstborn of his flock and from their fat,\" but all clean species are valid for them, as it is written (Genesis 8:20): \"and he took of every clean beast and of every clean bird and offered burnt offerings on the altar,\" and He added for Israel in the commandment that all their offerings be from cattle and from sheep, from turtledoves and from young pigeons. And the meaning of \"also of the fowl of the heaven\" — the clean ones, for Scripture continues from above."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:25:46.366008921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}